<title>ROMANIA: Romania six-month T-bill yield at 44.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Romania six-month T-bill yield at 44.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield of Romanian 182-day treasury bills was an annual 44.01 percent in Tuesday's auction with the finance ministry offer slightly oversubscribed by bids entered by 10 participants, the central bank (BNR) said.</p>
<p>The discount T-bills, the first longer maturity paper issued over the past year, have a 10 million lei face value and have been placed by the BNR through a single price auction. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>    Total on offer		512.99  billion lei</p>
<p>    Total bids received	 657.158 billion lei</p>
<p>    Total accepted bids	 512.992 billion lei</p>
<p>    Minimum price		  68.6556 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price		  88.7767 pct</p>
<p>    Accepted price		 81.8000 pct</p>
<p>    Annual yield		   44.01   pct</p>
<p>    Discount			 36.00   pct</p>
<p>    Maturity date	    5 Feb 1998 (182 days)</p>
<p>($=7,434 lei)</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
